# Corners minus edges plus faces: what does a cube give?
subtitle: "Count a cube's corners, edges and faces, type what V − E + F gives, and see why Euler's answer, 2, holds for every solid without holes."

## Corners minus edges plus faces: what does a cube give?
affirm: playful
text: {"font_size":32}
sources:
    - id: euler
      title: Euler's polyhedron formula
      authors: Plus Magazine, University of Cambridge
      year: 2007
      url: https://plus.maths.org/eulers-polyhedron-formula
      finding: V − E + F = 2 for every convex polyhedron; Euler stated it in a 1750 letter to Christian Goldbach

